ange my vote:** If another agent provides strong positive evidence of A\u2019s or D\u2019s teamwork and crew interaction that outweighs their negatives, or if B\u2019s communication flaws are shown to be critical safety risks, I would reconsider.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}", "thoughts": "We need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. We must follow round 1: provisional preference, not final. Use our info. We have candidate attributes list. Need to evaluate.\n\nWe have:\n\nCandidate A: can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Negatives: unfriendly, eats unhealthily.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills. Negatives: regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone when communicating.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Negatives: considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to weigh for long-distance pilot: reliability, responsibility, technical competence, calm under pressure, decision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nAssess each:\n\nA: strong anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership - good for safety, navigation. Weakness: unfriendly (teamwork), unhealthy eating (could affect stamina). No info on stress handling. Might be okay but teamwork concerns.\n\nB: conscientious, handles stress well, good weather assessment, computer skills (modern avionics). Weakness: pretentious, wrong tone - communication issues. But overall reliability high.\n\nC: quick correct decisions, excellent